  "query_preview": "..\n\nZonal flow over Montana will gradually build into an upper-level \nridge. Although minor perturbations moving through the flow will \nproduce elevated SE winds Monday, primarily fair weather is \nanticipated through Wednesday.\n\nBy Thursday, an upper-level low off the coast of central\nCalifornia will meander eastward over the Great Basin, enabling\nthe associated upper-level trough to begin digging over Montana. \nThe combination of trough-driven frontogenesis and moisture \nadvection will produce chances for precipitation beginning overnight\nThursday.\n\nAs of the most recent NBM run, precipitation is anticipated to \nend by Saturday morning. However, model agreement deteriorates \nsubstantially beyond this point. Forecast confidence is uncertain \nthrough the end of the week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Confidence in weather conditions is moderate to high through\n  Wednesday.\n\n- Confidence in precipitation late this week is low.\n\n- The GFS and ECMWF begin to exhibit significant discrepancies by\n  Friday morning. Both indicate upper-level troughing persisting\n  through Friday night, but orientation and strength vary.\n  \n\nDON",
